#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184010 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d88d6dd3-9da2-5bad-a373-7c62c3004b8b" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Quadratic “Or Equal To” Inequalities That Require Rearrangement"}] :question/id #uuid "fe8bd63f-87eb-5cc0-942c-011c3a59bc07" :question/math-academy-id "e-5063" :question/problem "Find the solution of $2x^2-6 \\le -4x$." :question/worked-solution "To solve this inequality using the graphical method, we first need to move all of the numbers to the left-hand side so that the right-hand side is $0$.\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}2x^{2} - 6 & \\le - 4x \\\\ 2x^{2} + 4x - 6 & \\le 0 \\\\ x^{2} + 2x - 3 & \\le 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nSo, we want to find the values of $x$ for which the parabola\n\n$$\ny=x^2+2x-3\n$$\n\nlies below the $x$-axis. Let's find the roots of the parabola by factoring:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nx^{2} + 2x - 3 &= 0 \\\\\n(x - 1)(x + 3) &= 0\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe see that the roots are $x=1$ and $x=-3$, and we can graph the parabola as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/3833/Source/Images/4927c4ddb9348af5ed197223c5719193.png)\n\nSince we are interested in solving\n\n$$\nx^2+2x-3 \\le 0\n$$\n\nwe look for the part of the parabola that is below the $x$-axis.\n\nBased on the graph, the solution is\n\n$$\n-3 \\le x \\le 1\n$$\n\nUsing interval notation, we write $x \\in [-3,1]$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184012 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ef5d4f19-5602-54a9-96ea-4e42054ff5c8" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Greater Than (Or Equal To) Inequalities"}] :question/id #uuid "d992e18d-b1b0-536e-a3fd-c1e66fc72a30" :question/math-academy-id "e-5186" :question/problem "Find the solution of $x^2-2x-8 \\geq 0$." :question/worked-solution "To solve the inequality\n\n$$\nx^2-2x-8 \\geq 0\n$$\n\nwe need to find the values of $x$ for which the parabola\n$y=x^2-2x-8$\nlies *above* the $x$-axis or touches this axis.\n\nFirst, let's find the roots of the parabola:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nx^{2} - 2x - 8 &= 0 \\\\\n(x + 2)(x - 4) &= 0\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the roots are $x=-2$ and $x=4$, and we can graph the parabola as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/3833/Source/Images/d48ff6ef1caea411bdbfb5e32821a420.png)\n\nThe values marked in blue show all $x$-values where the parabola lies *above* the axis or touches this axis.\n\nSo, the solution to the inequality is\n\n$$\nx \\leq -2\n$$\n\nor\n\n$$\nx \\geq 4\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184061 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "530fc010-b15b-5877-8ed6-7fd2f8feb37c" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Strict Quadratic Inequalities That Require Rearrangement"}] :question/id #uuid "187f0c0b-6e70-5c17-800e-8bf4dad6d5be" :question/math-academy-id "e-9936" :question/problem "Find the solution of $2x^2 < -4x$." :question/worked-solution "To solve this inequality using the graphical method, we first need to move all of the numbers to the left-hand side so that the right-hand side is $0$.\n$\\begin{bmatrix}2x^{2} & < - 4x \\\\ 2x^{2} + 4x & < 0\\end{bmatrix}$.\n\nSo, we want to find the values of $x$ for which the parabola\n\n$$\ny = 2x^2 + 4x\n$$\n\nlies below the $x$-axis. Let's find the roots of the parabola by factoring:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n2x^{2} + 4x &= 0 \\\\\n2x(x + 2) &= 0\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe see that the roots are $x = -2$ and $x = 0$, and we can graph the parabola as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/3833/Source/Images/bddb58670bbcb57b9f310b467227d839.png)\n\nSince we are interested in solving\n$2x^2 + 4x \\lt 0$,\nwe look for the part of the parabola that is below the $x$-axis.\n\nBased on the graph, the solution is $-2 < x < 0$.\n\nUsing interval notation, we write\n\n$$\nx \\in \\left(-2, 0\\right)\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184074 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cbe80595-c807-506c-a356-566f1edb3402" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Less Than (Or Equal To) Inequalities"}] :question/id #uuid "9eee913a-b3ce-5268-aa2d-09f5e97b0700" :question/math-academy-id "e-9977" :question/problem "Find the solution of $-x^2 + 7 x - 10 \\leq 0$." :question/worked-solution "To solve the inequality\n\n$$\n-x^2 + 7 x - 10 \\leq 0\n$$\n\nwe need to find the values of $x$ for which the parabola\n\n$$\ny = -x^2 + 7 x - 10\n$$\n\nlies *below* the $x$-axis or touches this axis.\n\nFirst, let's find the roots of the parabola:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-x^{2} + 7x - 10 &= 0 \\\\\n- (x^{2} - 7x + 10) &= 0 \\\\\n- (x - 2)(x - 5) &= 0\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the roots are $x=2$ and $x = 5$, and we can graph the parabola as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/3833/Source/Images/66589305706cca7f293953c16fb19690.png)\n\nThe values marked in blue show all $x$-values where the parabola lies *below* the $x$-axis or touches this axis.\n\nSo, the solution to the inequality is\n\n$$\nx \\leq 2\n$$\n\nor\n\n$$\nx \\geq 5\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184710 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d88d6dd3-9da2-5bad-a373-7c62c3004b8b" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Quadratic “Or Equal To” Inequalities That Require Rearrangement"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "89132c69-3565-5bf2-857b-18937f1dfa5b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x ∈ [- 1, \\frac{8}{3}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186183150} {:answer/id #uuid "95755705-5578-5ef9-82ba-43457bf7b2f4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x ∈ [- 4, \\frac{3}{2}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186183151} {:answer/id #uuid "1d11c011-de09-52b4-9385-2ca2f82c367b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x ∈ [- \\frac{1}{2}, 2]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186183152} {:answer/id #uuid "379d3b51-8701-523b-ad2d-ec5933cd9ccd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x ∈ [0, 2]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186183153} {:answer/id #uuid "4e9e0643-632f-5442-aba3-118bf6c32753" :answer/type